\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces The effect of provenance on ring widths (log(mm)). We report these intercept estimates as mean and 90\% uncertainty intervals (in square brackets) across our four different predictors (GDD: growing degree days, GSL: growing season length, SOS: start of season and EOS: end of season).}}{18}{table.caption.17}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces Summary output of each parameter from our four predictors, using ring width (log(mm)) as the response variable. We report estimates as mean and 90\% uncertainty intervals (in square brackets) across our four different predictors (GDD: growing degree days, GSL: growing season length, SOS: start of season and EOS: end of season). See `Data analyses' in Methods section for more details.}}{19}{table.caption.18}%
